cpp/ — optional C++ wrapper
===========================

Header-only wrapper around the librsvg-2.0 C API.  It is not compiled,
linked, or installed by `make` / `make install` / `make check`.
Nothing here changes rendering, CSS, limits, or the C ABI.

  librsvg.hpp  RAII `rsvg::Handle` (owns RsvgHandle, unrefs in the destructor)
  example.cpp  load, render_document, write a PNG

API
---

`rsvg::Handle` is a move-only owner of an `RsvgHandle`.  The destructor
calls `g_object_unref`.  Failures throw `rsvg::Error` (`std::runtime_error`).

Load: `from_file`, `from_data`, `from_gfile`, `from_stream`, `read_stream`.
Setup: `set_dpi`, `set_base_uri`, `set_base_gfile`, `set_stylesheet`,
`set_cancellable_for_rendering`.
Render: `render_document`, `render_layer`, `render_element`.
Geometry: `geometry_for_layer`, `geometry_for_element`,
`intrinsic_size_in_pixels`, `intrinsic_dimensions`, `has_sub`.

Example
-------

From this directory:

    c++ -std=c++11 -I. example.cpp \
        $(pkg-config --cflags --libs librsvg-2.0 cairo cairo-png)

Run from this directory so `../examples/icon.svg` is found.  The sample
loads that file, sets 96 DPI, queries pixel size, calls `render_document`,
and writes `example-out.png`.
